{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>But as for me</b> — He returns to what he began, <i>in the morning You hear my voice</i>, for he comes to the House of HaShem and has no offering with him, to bow down toward His sanctuary — like one who brings the first of the fruit of the earth, where it is written <i>and you shall bow down before YHWH your Elohim</i>. And the meaning is: I have no offering, only to give thanks for Your abundant kindness upon me." "And the meaning of <i>in Your fear</i> — I have nothing with which to bow down, only my fear of You, in the manner of <i>so that His fear may be upon your faces</i>, for the others fear HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:08.156545149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}